{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/981109-being-grappled-by-multiple-opponents","id":981109,"title":"Being grappled by multiple opponents?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-03T16:59:14-07:00","id":981109,"title":"Being grappled by multiple opponents?","content":"How would it work if a character is being grappled by multiple opponents, if all involved are trying to, say, bite each other, rather than hold or restrain?<br /> <br /> If character A is grappling with character B, and then character C also tries to grapple-attack character B, does character B get a contested roll against both the following turn? Or does character C get a free grapple move? <br /> <br /> Of course, it makes sense for one of A or C to restrain B for the other, but assuming they aren't working together and both want to hurt B, I'm not sure how this gets resolved mechanically.<br /> <br /> Can anyone explain it me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:32:57-07:00","id":981127,"title":"","content":"The base rule for multiple people in a grapple is to treat it as a teamwork action, so assuming both A and C want to injure B, have one of them roll and add their successes to the other's dicepool.<br /> <br /> This only applies if they're coordinated enough to help one another though. It's the simplest mechanical resolution, and the only one offered by the book, so let me spit ball some others.<br /> <br /> You could also have all three perform a contested roll. High roller gets one action (two on exceptional), low rollers get nothing. This keeps it pretty simple and gives B a fighting chance but not a great one. One person performs an action, one person is the victim of the action, and the third is unable to do anything mechanically significant in the chaos. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, if A and B are grappling and C wants to hurt B as well, it's easier to just make a normal attack. C retains Defense (probably at -1, I would count A as the 'first' attacker any round they grapple) unless C is the victim of Hold, Restrain, or Take Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:08:24-07:00","id":981194,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was originally going to put this in the Vampire section, as it involved multiple frenzying vampires, two of which were trying to bite the same target","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:32:01-07:00","id":981210,"title":"","content":"Ah, well, it's worth noting that Frenzying vamps bite on the same turn they establish a grapple, gain one vitae, and can feed on subsequent turns. This doesn't change much but it does mean the victim has one less turn to stave off exsanguination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}